completions_8:
1. First, calculate the total amount Mulan spent on jeans: 2 pairs * $30/pair = $60. 2. Then, calculate the total amount Mulan spent: $60 (jeans) + $20 (bag) = $80. 3. Next, calculate the total amount Mulan has: $40 (initial) + $100 (father) = $140. 4. Finally, calculate the amount of money Mulan has left: $140 (total) - $80 (spent) = $60.

So, Mulan has $60 left.
\boxed{60}

completions_6:
40*20 = 800; 800*0.1 = 80; 800 - 80 = 720; 720 + 800 = 1520
Rafaela received $20 per customer, and there were 40 customers. So Rafaela received 40 * $20 = $800 in tips. Julieta received 10% less money in tips than Rafaela, which means she received 10% less than $800. 10% of $800 is 0.10 * $800 = $80. So Julieta received $800 - $80 = $720 in tips. Altogether, Julieta and Rafaela received $720 + $800 = $1520 in tips.
\boxed{1520}

